---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const phone = "(833) 945-3473";
const phoneHref = "tel:+18339453473";
---

<Base
  title="Wildfire Defensible Space & Home Hardening Cost Guide 2026 — Western States"
  description="Complete cost guide for wildfire defensible space clearing, home hardening, and fire-resistant landscaping across California, Colorado, Oregon, Washington, and other Western states."
  canonical="https://westernwildfiredefense.com/cost/"
>

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Wildfire Mitigation Cost Guide — Western States 2026</h1>
      <p>Typical costs for defensible space clearing, home hardening, and fire-resistant landscaping by state and service type.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-section">

      <h2>Defensible Space Clearing Costs by State</h2>
      <p>Defensible space clearing costs depend on property size, vegetation type and density, terrain slope, and how much clearing has been done previously. The following ranges represent typical costs for a standard 1-acre property in each state.</p>

      <table class="cost-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>State</th><th>Avg. Clearing Cost (1 acre)</th><th>High-Risk Surcharge</th><th>Annual Maintenance</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>California</td><td class="cost-highlight">$2,800 – $8,500</td><td>+20–40% in VHFHSZ zones</td><td>$800 – $2,500/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Colorado</td><td class="cost-highlight">$2,200 – $7,000</td><td>+15–30% in WUI zones</td><td>$600 – $2,000/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Oregon</td><td class="cost-highlight">$2,000 – $6,500</td><td>+15–25% in high-risk zones</td><td>$500 – $1,800/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Washington</td><td class="cost-highlight">$1,800 – $6,000</td><td>+10–20% in SRA zones</td><td>$500 – $1,600/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Montana</td><td class="cost-highlight">$1,500 – $5,500</td><td>+10–20% in high-risk areas</td><td>$400 – $1,400/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Idaho</td><td class="cost-highlight">$1,400 – $5,000</td><td>+10–15% in WUI zones</td><td>$400 – $1,200/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Arizona</td><td class="cost-highlight">$1,600 – $5,500</td><td>+15–25% in high-risk zones</td><td>$450 – $1,500/yr</td></tr>
          <tr><td>New Mexico</td><td class="cost-highlight">$1,400 – $5,000</td><td>+10–20% in high-risk areas</td><td>$400 – $1,300/yr</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 style="margin-top:40px;">Home Hardening Costs</h2>
      <p>Home hardening involves upgrading the structure itself to resist ember intrusion and radiant heat. Costs vary significantly based on the age of the home, existing materials, and the scope of upgrades required.</p>

      <table class="cost-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Upgrade Type</th><th>Typical Cost</th><th>Priority Level</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Ember-resistant vent covers</td><td class="cost-highlight">$300 – $1,200</td><td>🔴 Critical</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Class A fire-rated roofing</td><td class="cost-highlight">$8,000 – $25,000</td><td>🔴 Critical</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Dual-pane tempered glass windows</td><td class="cost-highlight">$3,000 – $12,000</td><td>🟠 High</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Non-combustible deck replacement</td><td class="cost-highlight">$5,000 – $20,000</td><td>🟠 High</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Exterior wall siding upgrade</td><td class="cost-highlight">$8,000 – $30,000</td><td>🟡 Medium</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Garage door sealing</td><td class="cost-highlight">$500 – $2,000</td><td>🟠 High</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Full home hardening package</td><td class="cost-highlight">$8,000 – $35,000</td><td>Varies</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 style="margin-top:40px;">Grants & Rebates Available</h2>
      <p>Several state and federal programs offer financial assistance for wildfire mitigation work. Eligibility varies by state, income level, and property location.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>California:</strong> <a href="https://www.fire.ca.gov/programs/resource-management/grants/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CAL FIRE Grants Program</a> — up to $5,000 for qualifying homeowners</li>
        <li><strong>Colorado:</strong> <a href="https://dfpc.colorado.gov/wildfire-risk-reduction" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Colorado Wildfire Risk Reduction Program</a> — cost-share grants available</li>
        <li><strong>Oregon:</strong> <a href="https://www.oregon.gov/odf/fire/pages/defensiblespace.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oregon ODF Defensible Space Program</a> — technical assistance and rebates</li>
        <li><strong>Federal:</strong> <a href="https://www.usda.gov/topics/forestry/wildfire" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USDA Forest Service</a> — community wildfire defense grants</li>
      </ul>

      <div style="margin-top: 40px; text-align:center;">
        <a href={phoneHref} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">📞 Call {phone} — Free Assessment</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
